From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:40:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wineserver: report a thread in a syscall from its syscall
 frame

On iOS the server reads a suspended thread's registers through Mach. A
thread waiting in a syscall (WaitForSingleObject, Sleep) is in host
code then, and GetThreadContext returned a libsystem_kernel pc as rip
and its pthread stack as rsp. Upstream Wine's suspend handler reports
such a thread from its syscall frame (is_inside_syscall), the ARM64EC
state at the syscall: rip in ntdll, rsp on the guest's stack.

ios_fill_thread_context already did that, opt-in (MADEIRA_CTX_FRAME=1),
with a window read from TEB+0x3a8 as kernel_stack. Since Wine 11 the
thread data is no longer in the TEB, so that read gives nothing usable
and the substitution could not happen even when asked for. The window
is now the 1 MiB kernel stack below the syscall frame (TEB+0x378),
which alloc_syscall_frame puts at the kernel stack's top, and the
substitution is on by default. ntdll's ARM64EC code runs from a JIT-pool
copy, so the frame's pc is given as its PE address
(ios_jit_reverse_translate, as setup_exception gives an exception's).
The real-suspend safe-point test, which
reads the same field, is unchanged.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-guest-thread-context.md
Offered-upstream: no; the Mach capture is the iOS port's
---
 build/wineserver/mach_ios.c | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/wineserver/mach_ios.c b/build/wineserver/mach_ios.c
index 3b89323..ef2a49a 100644
--- a/build/wineserver/mach_ios.c
+++ b/build/wineserver/mach_ios.c
@@ -450,6 +450,8 @@ int send_thread_signal( struct thread *thread, int sig )
  * implausible value makes the whole substitution fall through. */
 #define IOS_TEB_SYSCALL_FRAME_OFF  0x378
 #define IOS_TEB_KERNEL_STACK_OFF   0x3a8
+/* kernel_stack_size (unix/unix_private.h): the syscall frame is at its top. */
+#define IOS_KERNEL_STACK_SIZE      0x100000
 /* struct syscall_frame (unix/signal_arm64.c): x[29] 000, fp 0e8, lr 0f0, sp 0f8,
  * pc 100, cpsr 108; sizeof == 0x330. */
 #define IOS_SCF_FP    0x0e8
@@ -1105,25 +1107,25 @@ int ios_fill_thread_context( struct thread *thread,
      * RtlIsEcCode() is deliberately not called here: that is a PE-side export and this is
      * native Unix code (ml613). The frame PC is classified later, in the EC wrapper.
      *
-     * Opt-in via MADEIRA_CTX_FRAME=1 while it is unproven. Every validation failure falls
-     * through to the old behaviour rather than inventing state. */
+     * Every validation failure falls through to the old behaviour rather than inventing
+     * state.
+     *
+     * PLA-245: on by default (it was opt-in, MADEIRA_CTX_FRAME=1), and the window is the
+     * 1 MiB kernel stack below the syscall frame. Since Wine 11 the thread data, and
+     * with it kernel_stack, is no longer in the TEB, so TEB+0x3a8 read nothing usable
+     * and the substitution never happened: a thread waiting in a syscall reported its
+     * host pc and pthread stack. The frame is at the top of the kernel stack
+     * (alloc_syscall_frame), and a nested callback's frame is below the previous one. */
     if (have_native)
     {
-        static int ctx_frame_env = -1;
-        if (ctx_frame_env < 0)
-        {
-            const char *e = getenv( "MADEIRA_CTX_FRAME" );
-            ctx_frame_env = (e && e[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0;
-        }
-        if (ctx_frame_env && thread->teb)
+        if (thread->teb)
         {
-            uint64_t frame = 0, kstack = 0;
+            uint64_t frame = 0;
             uint64_t sp = native->ctl.arm64_regs.sp;
             uint64_t mach_pc = native->ctl.arm64_regs.pc;   /* before substitution */
             if (ios_safe_read( (uint64_t)thread->teb + IOS_TEB_SYSCALL_FRAME_OFF, &frame, 8 ) &&
-                ios_safe_read( (uint64_t)thread->teb + IOS_TEB_KERNEL_STACK_OFF, &kstack, 8 ) &&
-                frame && kstack && !(frame & 7) && kstack < frame &&
-                sp >= kstack && sp <= frame)
+                frame > IOS_KERNEL_STACK_SIZE && !(frame & 7) &&
+                sp > frame - IOS_KERNEL_STACK_SIZE && sp <= frame)
             {
                 unsigned char f[IOS_SCF_SIZE];
                 if (ios_safe_read( frame, f, sizeof(f) ))
@@ -1140,6 +1142,14 @@ int ios_fill_thread_context( struct thread *thread,
                             native->integer.arm64_regs.x19[i - 19] = *(uint64_t *)(f + i * 8);
                         native->integer.arm64_regs.x19[10] = *(uint64_t *)(f + IOS_SCF_FP);
                         native->integer.arm64_regs.x19[11] = *(uint64_t *)(f + IOS_SCF_LR);
+                        /* PLA-245: ntdll's ARM64EC code runs from a JIT-pool copy; the
+                         * caller is given its PE address, as setup_exception gives an
+                         * exception's. */
+                        {
+                            extern uint64_t ios_jit_reverse_translate( uint64_t addr, uint64_t *module_base );
+                            uint64_t pe = ios_jit_reverse_translate( fpc, NULL );
+                            if (pe) fpc = pe;
+                        }
                         native->ctl.arm64_regs.sp     = fsp;
                         native->ctl.arm64_regs.pc     = fpc;
                         native->ctl.arm64_regs.pstate = *(uint32_t *)(f + IOS_SCF_CPSR);
